          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_dglie_algebras In dg-Lie algebras
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}, [-,-],\partial)
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            of degree -1), a
            %strong Maurer-Cartan element
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathfrak{g}_1
                of degree -1
            %li
              %p
                such that the
                %strong Maurer-Cartan equation
                holds
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\partial a + \frac{1}{2}[a,a] = 0
                      \\,.
          %p
            This is a special case of MC elements for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
          %h3#InLInfinityAlgebras
            In
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            with brackets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,\cdots,-]_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathfrak{g}
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sum_{k = 0}^\infty \frac{1}{k!} [a, \cdots, a]_k
                  \=
                  0
                  \\,.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#AsHomomorphisms
            As
            = succeed "-homomorphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes \mathfrak{g}
            naturally inherits the structure of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            be of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes \mathfrak{g}
            correspond bijectively to dg-algebra homomorphisms
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ←
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \leftarrow CE(\mathfrak{g})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi dgAlg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MC(A \otimes \mathfrak{g})
                  \\simeq
                  Hom_{dgAlg}(CE(\mathfrak{g}), A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            A reference for this is for instance around def. 3.1 in (
            %a{:href => "#Hain"}> Hain 1983
            ).
          %p We unwind in steps how this comes about:
          %p
            First, the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ←
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A  \leftarrow CE(\mathfrak{g})
            is a subspace of the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{CE}(\mathfrak{g})
            is freely generated as a graded algebra and is of finite type by assumption, this is isomorphic to the space of grading preserving homomorphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathrm{Vect}[{\mathbb{Z}]}}(\mathfrak{g}^*,A)
          %p
            of linear grading-preserving maps from the graded vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            of dual generators to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Vect}[\mathbb{Z}]
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            of finite type, this is isomorphic to the space of elements of total degree degree 1 in elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            tensored with
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A \otimes \mathfrak{g})_1
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathrm{Vect}[{\mathbb{Z}]}}(\mathfrak{g}^*,A)
                  \\,.
          %p The dg-algebra homomorphism form the subspace of this space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mi dgAlg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mi grAlg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{Hom}_{dgAlg}(\mathrm{CE}(\mathfrak{g}),A)
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\mathrm{Hom}_{grAlg}(\mathrm{CE}(\mathfrak{g}),A)
                  \\simeq
                  (A \otimes \mathfrak{g})_1
          %p
            on elements that respect the differential. Under the above equivalence this are elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \otimes \mathfrak{g})_1
            satisfying a certain condition. By inspection one finds that this condition is precisely the MC equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_A A + \partial a  + [a \cdot_A a]_2 + [a \cdot_A a \cdot_A a ]_3
                  + \cdots = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \Omega^\bullet(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+algebra"} de Rham algebra
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MC(A \otimes \mathfrak{g})
            is the space of flat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebroid-valued+differential+form"} L-∞ algebra valued differential forms
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X) \otimes \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            A Maurer-Cartan element is then precisely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+1-form"} Lie algebra valued 1-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form vanishes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{dR} A + [A \wedge A] = 0
                  \\,.
          %h2#range_of_versions_and_applications Range of versions and applications
          %p
            %em Maurer–Cartan equation
            is a name for very many related equations in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan forms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisting+cochain"} twisting cochains
          %p
            A Maurer–Cartan equation for
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity-algebra"} algebra
            %em generalized Maurer–Cartan equation
            as it has more summands than the one for
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity-category"} categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
            algebra are called Maurer-Cartan elements.
          %h2#maurercartan_and_lie_theory Maurer-Cartan and Lie theory
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sophus+Lie"} Sophus Lie
            considered groups of transformations first and discovered
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lie+group"} local Lie group
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie%27s+three+theorems"} third Lie theorem
          %h2#references References
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ludwig+Maurer"}> Ludwig Maurer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Über allgemeinere Invarianten-Systeme
              %strong 18
              (1888), 103-150.
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#Nakahara03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikio+Nakahara"}> Mikio Nakahara
                , Section 5.6.4 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometry%2C+Topology+and+Physics"} Geometry, Topology and Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9781315275826"} doi:10.1201/9781315275826
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://alpha.sinp.msu.ru/~panov/LibBooks/GRAV/(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)Mikio_Nakahara-Geometry,_Topology_and_Physics,_Second_Edition_(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)-Institute_of_Physics_Publishing(2003).pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"}> Martin Markl
                , Def. 3.11 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation theory of algebras and their diagrams
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 116
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=CBMS-116"} ISBN:978-0-8218-8979-4
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.gbv.de/dms/goettingen/721467989.pdf"} toc pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerd+Rudolph"}> Gerd Rudolph
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Schmidt"} Matthias Schmidt
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Geometry and Mathematical Physics Part II. Fibre Bundles, Topology and Gauge Fields
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-94-024-0959-8"} doi:10.1007/978-94-024-0959-8
          %p
            A MathOverflow entry about Maurer-Cartan forms for Lie groups:
            %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/34418/maurer-cartan-form"} maurer-cartan-form
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie%27s+third+theorem"} Lie's third theorem
            from the point of view of Maurer–Cartan equations:
          %ul
            %li
              %p Sigurdur Helgason, Differential geometry, Lie groups, and symmetric spaces
            %li
              %p N. Bourbaki, Lie algebras and lie groups, historical appendix
            %li
              %p F. Engel, P. Heegaard, Sophus Lie Samlede Avhandliger (Collected works)
          %p
            In the generality of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Doubek"}> Martin Doubek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"} Martin Markl
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Petr+Zima"} Petr Zima
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation Theory (lecture notes)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.3719"} arXiv:0705.3719
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrey+Lazarev"}> Andrey Lazarev
                , Def. 5.1 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Maurer-Cartan moduli and models for function spaces
                = succeed "," do
